      simpleExplanation: "Shari'ah is the complete code of divine guidance for how Muslims should live, covering beliefs, personal discipline, social/economic rules, duties and prohibitions. Its rules come primarily from the Qur'an and the Prophet's example (Sunnah); when new situations arise that these don't directly address, scholars use consensus (Ijma'a) and reasoned analogy (Qiyas), guided by scholarly effort (Ijtihad).",
